- F-34 **Against the interpreter's library, on the code of `832f7d0d91`, the code generator refuses 24 declarations of the fourteen components that the distance stage checks, in 8 kinds, all of them declarations that the checker passes; the count can be taken only on a patched tree.** The setting is the distance stage's (F-53): the checker's failures caught per declaration, and the bound `Any`. On that code without the patch, the code generator stops `FortressLibrary`, `FortressBuiltin` and `FlatString` whole at the wrappers of their helper classes (row 874). So the measure's script first applies a patch in a scratch worktree: naming tables and converters for the one library's built-in types, the trait table's search over its two prelude apis (row 942), and `NN32`'s two getters at `NN32` (row 993). Then: 24 refused, 745 emitted, no component failure. By row: varargs 8, one of them a trait's (row 624); `label` 4 (row 81, fixed since); a type variable missing from the kind environment 4 (rows 822 and 812); the range operators over pairs and triples 4 (row 819, fixed since); a closure class written twice 2 (row 315); an intersection as a receiver 1 (row 540); `atomic` as an expression 1 (row 875, fixed since). A declaration counts at its first wall, and some hold a second: behind `SubString`'s `label` stands the partial type assumption (row 818). The measure skips the dispatch methods. It sees no class that is emitted and fails when it loads; the four such walls of that code, rows 990, 991, 992 and 732, are fixed since. No emitted class of the measure is run, and no test checks the count, since the gate's distance stage runs no code generation. So after the switch-over the code generator still stands between the library and bytecode. Measured twice on the code of `832f7d0d91`, with one result. On the code of `7858d0e97b`, with rows 81 and 875 fixed, the same script gave 21 refused, measured once: varargs 10, two of them declarations that met `label` or `atomic` first; the kind environment 4; the range operators 4; a closure class written twice 2; an intersection as a receiver 1. No count is taken on later code. Command: `explorations/compile-ladder/plan-31/probes/planner/codegen-measure.sh <scratch-worktree> <out-dir>`. Detail: `compile-ladder/plan-31/PROBES.md`, "3. The measure: the declarations of the fourteen components that the code generator refuses"; `compile-ladder/plan-31/probes/switch-rehearsal.md`, "3. The code generator over the library today, against F-34"; `reviews/batch-31b-review.md`, section 3.
  from: explorations/reviews/batch-31b-review.md, "3. The measure: the declarations of the one library that the code generator refuses"; from: explorations/reviews/batch-31b-review.md, "Corrections owed in the record"; commit: 00dd16a89; note: the pass at climb batch 31b's landing: the count of 21 on `7858d0e97b`, measured by run 2's base-build worker at 06:46 to 06:49 UTC on 2026-11-17 before climb batch 31b's rungs, replaces the clause that said no count was taken with rows 81 and 875 fixed; no stage measured it after climb batch 31b; to make room, the unpatched figure of eleven components moved to PROBES.md section 3, and the kinds of the four load-time walls (rows 990, 991, 992, 732) to that section and switch-rehearsal.md section 3; the words on the trait's varargs kept, since they make the eighth kind

- F-229 **`array1` and `array2` give a vector and a matrix only at the eight number types, chosen by a `typecase` over a witness of their result type; at any other element type they give a plain array.** The branches are `ZZ32`, `ZZ64`, `NN32`, `NN64`, `ZZ`, `QQ`, `RR32` and `RR64`; each builds the array at that type and returns it through `cast`, in `additiveIdentity`'s shape. `Array1` and `Array2` are invariant, so a branch matches only its own number type exactly. `Number` and `AnyIntegral` get a plain array, since `Vector[\Number,n\]` is not well-formed under the element bound `T extends { Number, MultiplicativeRing[\T\] }` of `Vector` and `Matrix` (F-151). The specification's "Array Expressions" makes an array of `Number` elements a vector (row 729, contested). Under walk, a type parameter inferred from a `ZZ32`, `ZZ64` or `RR64` value is that type, so it gets a vector (`tests/ArrayInferredElementVectorWalk`). The witness is of the result type because a witness of the element type failed while walk's `ZZ32` values were of a native object `Int`, now gone (F-379): at `T = Int`, `() -> Int` matched the `ZZ32` branch, and the `cast` of the `ZZ32` vector to an array of `Int` threw `CastError` (row 722, the same cast in `openRange`). Gated under walk by `tests/ArrayFactoryNumberTypes` and `ArrayFactoryAbstractNumber`. The distance stage measures the compiled checker's acceptance; it reports, and does not turn the gate red. Detail: `compile-ladder/rung-library-factories/REPORT.md` sections 1 (the change), 3 and 4 (the ways measured).
  from: explorations/compile-ladder/rung-number-objects/REPORT.md, "What changed and why"; commit: 00dd16a89; note: the pass at climb batch 31b's landing: the reason for the witness told in the past, without the words "before F-379", since rung O of climb batch 31b removed walk's native object `Int`

- F-299 **Walk loads a `builtinPrimitive` string that names a static helper of `nativeHelpers/` beside its glue classes, and 373 of the one library's 401 live bindings name one.** It builds P-58, "Every native binding is a ...", whose compiled half F-298 gives. The loader (`interpreter/glue/StaticNativeApp.java`) calls the overload whose Java types carry the declared types, `self` first, and raises a helper's `fortress.<Api>$<Name>` as the library's `<Name>`. It refuses at load a string that names no helper or fits none, and a declared type that no Java type carries, `self`'s among them, read from the declaring type. For 15 names it runs walk's own operations instead and loads no helper: eight by the table `OWN_OPERATIONS` of `interpreter/glue/NativeApp.java`, `stringOps.typeName` and `equality.sEquiv` (F-328) and `runtime`'s six (F-335), and `arrayOps`' seven by one rule (F-333). The library's own `FlatString`, identified by the component that declares it, carries `self` in a Java `String`; a program's own type named `FlatString` or `JavaString` carries none. The `fortress-repo` skill's `references/interpreter.md`, "Natives", gives the carriers, the messages, the refusal of a helper parameter declared `String`, and the loader's departures (rows 864, 551 and 846). The 373 by type: `ZZ32` 32, `ZZ64` 31 and `ZZ` 28 (F-306, F-327, F-331; their `CHOOSE` F-305, `REM` and `MOD` F-312, divisors F-314), `RR64` 61 and the top-level `fromRawBits` (F-303, F-323), `RR32` 51 (F-310, its `asFloat` F-311), the `asFloat`s of `ZZ64` and `ZZ` 2 (F-311), the small rest 8 (F-307), the two that round a numeral once into `RR64` and `RR32` (F-79), and `NN32` 30, `NN64` 31 (its 32nd binding, `signed`, counted with the small rest) and `Char` 40 (F-308, F-313, F-327, F-331), the top-level `nanoTime` (F-314) and `random` (F-323), `Object`'s `ilkName` and `SEQV` over `Any` (F-328), `JavaBufferedWriter`'s 7 (F-330), `JavaBufferedReader`'s 10 (F-332), the array stores' 7 (F-333), `runtime`'s 6 (F-335), `System`'s `args` 2 (F-337), and the string family's 20: `FlatString`'s 13 methods; `natLineSeparator`; `match`; and `printThreadInfo`, `printWithThread`, `printlnWithThread`, `getEnvironment` and `getProperty`, each a native over `FlatString` beside an overload over `String` that flattens in a `typecase`. The other 28 name glue classes, `Reflect`'s (F-32). Test: `tests/NativeHelperBindingWalk.fss`, `NativeHelperRaiseWalk`, `ZZ32DivisionByZeroWalk`, `NativeHelperFamilyZZ32Walk`, `NativeHelperCarriedSelfFlatStringWalk`, `NativeHelperStringRopeWalk`, `compiler_tests/NativeHelperFamilyStringCompiled`, and the refusals `NativeHelperMisspeltWalk`, `NativeHelperMisfitWalk`, `NativeHelperUncarriedWalk`, `NativeHelperUncarriedSelf*Walk` and `NativeHelperNonFlatStringWalk`; the entries of the other families name their own tests. Detail: `compile-ladder/rung-number-objects/REPORT.md`, "What changed and why", for the count of 373 of 401; `compile-ladder/climb-batch-28/RECORD.md`, "The count of the bindings"; `compile-ladder/rung-natives-walk/REPORT.md`, "What changed and why"; `compile-ladder/rung-natives-self/REPORT.md`, "What changed and why"; `compile-ladder/rung-string-natives/REPORT.md`, "What changed and why".
  from: compile-ladder/climb-batch-31b/RECORD.md, "FACTS entries"; from: explorations/compile-ladder/rung-number-objects/REPORT.md, "What changed and why"; commit: 00dd16a89; note: the pass at climb batch 31b's landing: the count's source, rung O's report, added to the Detail; what `NN64`'s 31 counts, from the gather's record line for F-299; checked at 00dd16a89, 32 `builtinPrimitive` bindings in the object `NN64` (`Library/FortressLibrary.fss:1063-1168`); F-308's `NN64` 30 counts another partition

- F-308 **A `builtinPrimitive` binding over `NN32`, `NN64` or `Char` whose helper takes or answers a Java `int` or `long` compiles on the compiled path through the six transfer helpers, and `NN32`'s 30, `NN64`'s 30 (by this entry's count; F-299 counts 31 of the object's 32) and `Char`'s 40 bindings name their helpers.** Where the declaration says `NN32`, `NN64` or `Char`, and the helper has an `int` or a `long`, the rewrite of F-298 wraps that argument, or the call, in the matching transfer, as the compiler's prelude does; walk needs none. A helper overloaded at its arity gets no transfer (row 885), nor does `self` in a generic owner; the declared type is read by its simple name (row 886). The transfers are identities, so the checker passes whatever the helper computes: a binding over `NN32` to the signed `simpleIntArith.intLT` compiles and answers `true` for 2^31 < 1, as walk does; only the walk and compiled guards check that each of them but `Char`'s `asExprString` and F-327's six shifts and powers, which its own tests check, names the unsigned helper. Under walk those 93 keep the glue classes' values, but `NN32`'s and `NN64`'s `DIV`, `REM` and `MOD` by zero throw `DivisionByZero`. All 100 bindings over these types name helpers, `NN64`'s `asFloat` at `RR64` among them; `Char`'s `asExprString` names `simpleChar.charToExprString` (F-329). The `fortress-repo` skill's `references/compiler.md`, "Natives", names the transfers. Test: `compiler_tests/NativeHelperTransferCompiled`; the guards `NativeHelperFamilyNN32Compiled`, `NativeHelperFamilyNN64Compiled`, `NativeHelperFamilyCharCompiled`, `NativeHelperFamilyAsFloatCompiled`, `NativeHelperFamilyUnsignedCompiled` and `tests/NativeHelperFamilyNN32Walk`, `NativeHelperFamilyUnsignedWalk`, `NativeHelperFamilyNN64Walk`, `NativeHelperFamilyCharWalk`; `tests/NN32DivisionByZeroWalk`, `NN64DivisionByZeroWalk`. Detail: `compile-ladder/climb-batch-27/RECORD.md`, "The count of the bindings"; `compile-ladder/rung-natives-hard/REPORT.md`, "1. What changed and why"; `compile-ladder/rung-natives-hard/SKEPTIC.md`, "The failure mode".
